    17	    17	# Langfuse
    18	    18	
    19	    19	This skill helps you use Langfuse effectively across all common workflows: instrumenting applications, migrating prompts, debugging traces, and accessing data programmatically.
    20	    20	
    21	    21	## Core Principles
    22	    22	
    23	    23	Follow these principles for ALL Langfuse work:
    24	    24	
    25	    25	1. **Documentation First**: NEVER implement based on memory. Always fetch current docs before writing code (Langfuse updates frequently) See the section below on how to access documentation.
    26	    26	2. **CLI for Data Access**: Use `langfuse-cli` when querying/modifying Langfuse data. See the section below on how to use the CLI.
    27	    27	3. **Best Practices by Use Case**: Check the relevant reference file below for use-case-specific guidelines before implementing
    28	    28	4. **Use latest Langfuse versions**: Unless the user specified otherwise or there's a good reason, always use the latest version of Langfuse SDKs/APIs. Even if you're only creating a plan for another agent to execute, be explicit about the exact version to use.
    29	    29	5. **If you guide the user through UI** and are unsure about a label or location, inspect the user’s screenshots or ask to see the relevant screen. Do not assume UI labels have the exact same names as API, SDK, or CLI fields.
